            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jillian"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Wow! This definitely is some of the \"Best BBQ Shrimp Ever\"! I did cut way back on the oil though...only using a little over 1/4 cup. I used olive oil vs. canola and 1/4 tsp. of tabasco. I also added a little chili garlic sauce and a splash of white wine vinegar. I let this marinate about 4 hours and these were fabulous! Thanks for a great recipe Huge!",
            "datePublished": "2011-09-01T10:19:23.503Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "AdventurousPalate"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I was a little concerned with how spicy this recipe would be when reading through the ingredients but was surprised at how subtle the flavour was when the shrimp were cooked! I happened to have fresh oregano in our herb garden and used that instead of the dried version. Also substituted the tomato based chili (realized at the last minute that I didn’t have any) with a combination of sweet chili sauce and ketchup....which seemed to be ok. A great summer bbq recipe that we’ll be trying again!",
            "datePublished": "2018-05-21T05:00:21.627Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
